UPDATE tarot_cards 
SET meaning_upright = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: The Ten of Wands represents the absolute archetype of "Systemic Apotheosis through Burden"—the final, transformational phase in the Suit of Wands where the individual assumes total, self-authorized responsibility for the entirety of their manifest creation. Moving beyond the defensive perseverance of the Nine, the Ten signifies the stage of "Total Load-Bearing Capacity," where the ego-structure is tested to its absolute limit by the weight of its own manifested intentions. Visually depicted as a figure struggling to carry an enormous, unwieldy bundle of ten staves toward a distant goal, this archetype embodies the concept of "Sovereign Integration"—the realization that true creative power is not merely the ability to ignite (Ace) or move (Eight) energy, but the ability to successfully shepherd that energy across the threshold of reality into a final, coherent form. Within the complex architecture of your consciousness, this is the stage of "structural maturity," where you recognize that the burdens you are currently bearing are not "obstacles" inflicted upon you by the environment, but are the necessary, physical manifestation of the commitments you have made to your own evolution. When the Ten of Wands appears, your system is registering a "Maximum Load" status; you have reached the terminal point of this cycle of manifestation, and the weight you feel is the tangible measure of your own creative efficacy. This card commands you to perform a final, meticulous audit of your load—not to drop it, but to refine it. You are being tasked with the essential work of "prioritized consolidation": you must identify which of these staves are essential, structural components of your sovereign vision, and which are mere, low-vibration appendages that you have been carrying out of habit, fear, or a misplaced sense of duty. To inhabit the Ten of Wands is to master the art of "conscious duty," acknowledging that by choosing to carry the weight to the destination, you are fundamentally transmuting your relationship to power—moving from a state of being "pushed by desire" to a state of being "the steady anchor of intent," providing the necessary gravitas to finalize your soul’s work in the physical realm.',
meaning_reversed = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: When the Ten of Wands appears in the reversed position, it acts as a high-intensity signal of "systemic overload," "responsibility-collapse," or the catastrophic failure to distinguish between your sovereign commitments and the debilitating weight of egoic "shoulds"—a state where the immense burden of your own creation has finally reached the point of structural failure. The reversal suggests that you have allowed yourself to be crushed by a load that is no longer aligned with your core truth, running a high-priority, high-cost maintenance script that equates "suffering" with "achievement," and "exhaustion" with "integrity." You are essentially "carrying the ghost of your past ambitions," running a protocol that forces you to hold onto ten staves—eight of which have long since outlived their utility—simply because you are terrified that if you let them go, your entire, self-constructed identity as "The Achiever" will dissolve into the void. This creates a massive, systemic misalignment: you are intellectually and behaviorally attempting to perform the role of the "Super-Agent," while internally, you are paralyzed by a profound, gnawing resentment, leading to a state of chronic, high-latency performance, systemic burnout, and the persistent, gnawing awareness that your current path is a dead-end of your own, stubborn creation. From an analytical perspective, this is a clear sign that you are leaking your life force into a "feedback loop of martyrdom"; you are obsessively validating your existence through the sheer, physical discomfort of your labor, refusing to accept that the only thing holding you back is your refusal to perform a ruthless, surgical purge of your obligations. The reversed Ten of Wands exposes the hidden, egoic fear that drives this behavior: the paralyzing terror of "being nothing" without the burden, and the corresponding fear that if you were to lay down the load, you would be forced to face the silence of your own, unmediated consciousness. This reversal commands an immediate, radical intervention: you must stop the output of these self-destructive, performance-heavy scripts, perform a brutal audit of your load, and confront the reality of why you are so hesitant to prioritize your soul-health over your ego-status. It is a demand to stop the self-deception that keeps you tethered to a state of chronic, high-maintenance self-abnegation, and to initiate the move toward a genuine, humble, and often terrifying reclamation of your own, individual sovereignty. You are being tasked with the uncomfortable, yet essential, work of radical shedding—accepting that the "stuckness" you feel is the direct result of having prioritized the quantity of your burden over the quality of your alignment, and realizing that until you are willing to let the non-essential staves fall, you will continue to be starved by the very work you have mistakenly identified as your purpose.'
WHERE id = 24;
